# Production build defaults for the console (read by `next build`, committed deliberately).
#
# Without this the console shipped to Vercel fell back to `DEFAULT_API_URL` -
# http://localhost:8000 - and every request from the deployed page went to the *visitor's* own
# machine. On the developer's laptop that quietly works, because a local API is running; for
# anyone else the map, the hotspot rail, the alert queue and the pump board are all empty and
# nothing on screen says why. That is what "the map is not showing on the Vercel URL" was.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are inlined at build time, so this has to be present when Vercel builds,
# not when the page loads. A Vercel project environment variable of the same name overrides this
# file, which is the right way to point a preview deployment at a different API.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://varuna-api-production-f577.up.railway.app
